<header class="page-header">
  <div class="container page-header__inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">What this site collects, and what it doesn't.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Last updated 10 September 2026.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>This website is operated by Misinfo Trace. It is hosted by Netlify.</p>

    <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>If you subscribe to updates:</strong> your email address.</li>
      <li><strong>If you use the contact form:</strong> your name, email address, what you work on if you choose to say, and your message.</li>
      <li><strong>When you visit any page:</strong> our host keeps standard server logs, which include your IP address and the page requested. We use Netlify's server-side analytics to count page views from those logs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="not">What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We set no cookies.</li>
      <li>We run no tracking or advertising scripts, and no third-party analytics.</li>
      <li>The page loads nothing from other services — fonts included — so visiting it tells no one but our host.</li>
      <li>We don't sell or share your information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
    <p>Email addresses from the signup form are used only to send project updates. Contact messages are used to reply to you. Page-view counts tell us, in aggregate, which pages people read.</p>

    <h2 id="processors">Who else handles it</h2>
    <p>Form submissions and server logs are stored by Netlify, which hosts the site, under <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify's privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to remove your email address from updates, or to delete anything you have sent us, through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. We keep submissions only as long as we need them for the purpose you sent them for.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new date.</p>
  </div>
</div>
